From: Neo-PiOS <neopios@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] meson: fix aml pkg-config name (aml1 not aml)

The aml library (v1.0.0) provides pkg-config file named 'aml1' not 'aml'
(filebase: 'aml1' in aml/meson.build -> aml1.pc). Weston's VNC backend
meson.build looks for dependency('aml') but should look for
dependency('aml1') to match the actual pkg-config filename (as already
fixed in neatvnc via 0001-meson-Use-new-pkgconfig-for-aml1.patch).

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Neo-PiOS <neopios@example.com>
---
 libweston/backend-vnc/meson.build | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libweston/backend-vnc/meson.build b/libweston/backend-vnc/meson.build
index 1234567..abcdefg 100644
--- a/libweston/backend-vnc/meson.build
+++ b/libweston/backend-vnc/meson.build
@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@
 	error('VNC backend requires neatvnc which was not found. Or, you can use \'-Dbackend-vnc=false\'.')
 endif
 
-dep_aml = dependency('aml', version: ['>= 0.3.0', '< 0.4.0'], required: false, fallback: ['aml', 'aml_dep'])
+dep_aml = dependency('aml1', version: ['>= 0.3.0', '< 2.0.0'], required: false, fallback: ['aml', 'aml_dep'])
 if not dep_aml.found()
 	error('VNC backend requires libaml which was not found. Or, you can use \'-Dbackend-vnc=false\'.')
 endif
